# ELI End User Licence Agreement

**Copyright © 2026 Jason Fitzgibbon Bridgeman. All rights reserved.**

> **Status: draft for solicitor review.** These are the intended terms for ELI v3 and the official
> ELI bundles. The binding version is the one presented at purchase. Purchase date and receipt govern
> your grant.
>
> **Open items before launch** (marked **[to confirm]** below): governing law and courts (§17), the
> security-support window after the next major version (§4.4), and review of the warranty and
> liability wording for each country ELI is sold in (§§13–14).

---

## Plain-English summary

This summary is here to help you. It is not part of the legal terms; the numbered sections are.

- **You pay once.** There is no subscription. The version you bought keeps working for as long as you
  want to use it.
- **Every 3.x update is included.** Buying ELI v3 covers every 3.x release. ELI v4 will be a
  separate, paid upgrade. You keep the right to use v3 after v4 comes out.
- **No internet needed to keep using it.** Your licence key is checked on your own machine. ELI does
  not contact a licence server when it starts, and it never sends us your conversations, memories or
  files.
- **If we disappear, your copy still works.** There is no licence server for your copy to depend on.
- **Reinstalling is fine.** You can reinstall, and you can move your licence to a replacement machine.
- **How many machines:** the number on your receipt for your tier (see the tier supplements in
  `docs/eula/`).
- **Your data is yours.** We claim no rights in anything you create or store with ELI.
- **Bundles are separate products.** ELI Legal, ELI VR and the other official bundles are bought
  separately, each with its own price and its own schedule of terms, unless your ELI v3 licence
  includes them (your receipt says so).
- **You may not** share your key, resell or redistribute ELI, or run it as a service for other
  people unless your licence says you can.

---

## 1. Definitions

- **"We", "us", "the Licensor":** Jason Fitzgibbon Bridgeman.
- **"You":** the person or organisation that purchased the licence, or that is using a trial.
- **"ELI Product":** ELI v3 and each official ELI bundle or add-on we publish, such as ELI Legal,
  ELI VR, ELI Healthcare, ELI Finance and ELI Creation Station. Each one is a separate ELI Product.
- **"Software":** the ELI Product you have licensed, in the form we supply it, including updates we
  provide under §4 and its documentation.
- **"Licence Key":** the signed key we issue for a purchase. It identifies the ELI Product, its
  major version, your tier and your number of machines or seats.
- **"Major Version Line":** all releases that share a major version number, for example ELI v3.0
  through 3.x. For an ELI Product whose releases are numbered below 1.0, the releases before 1.0
  belong to its 1.x line.
- **"Tier Supplement":** the terms for your licence tier (Personal, Pro, Enterprise, Trial) in
  `docs/eula/`.
- **"Product Schedule":** the additional terms for one official bundle in `docs/eula/bundles/`.
- **"Your Data":** everything you put into the Software or produce with it, including files,
  conversations, memories, generated documents, settings and models you supply.
- **"Marketplace Package":** a plugin, MCP server, bundle, integration or other package published by
  someone other than us, whether or not it is listed on the ELI marketplace.

## 2. How these terms fit together

Your licence for an ELI Product is made up of:

1. this agreement;
2. the Tier Supplement for the tier you bought; and
3. for an official bundle, that bundle's Product Schedule.

Your order or receipt states the ELI Product, tier and number of machines or seats, and any
official bundles your ELI v3 licence includes. If documents conflict, the Product Schedule prevails
for its own product, then the Tier Supplement, then this agreement.

## 3. Licence grant

3.1 **Grant.** When you have paid for an ELI Product, we grant you a non-exclusive, perpetual licence
to install and use the Software for that product's Major Version Line, on the number of machines or
seats stated in your Licence Key and receipt, for the uses your Tier Supplement permits.

3.2 **Perpetual.** Your licence does not expire because time passes or because any billing
relationship ends. It ends only as described in §12.

3.3 **Licensed, not sold.** The Software is licensed to you, not sold. We keep all rights we do not
expressly grant, including copyright and all other intellectual property in the Software.

3.4 **Modification.** You may modify the Software for your own use on your licensed machines. That
includes changes ELI makes to its own code at your request. You may not distribute modified copies.

3.5 **Machines and seats.** The limit on machines or seats is part of your licence even where the
Software does not enforce it technically. Replacing a machine and moving the licence to the new one
is not an extra machine.

3.6 **Transfer.** You may transfer your whole licence to another person or organisation only with our
written consent, which we will not unreasonably withhold. After a transfer you must stop using the
Software and give the Licence Key to the new holder.

3.7 **Trials.** A trial licence lasts for the period in the Trial supplement. It is for evaluation
only and ends automatically at the end of that period.

3.8 **Included bundles.** Where your ELI v3 licence includes an official bundle, you also receive the
licence in §3.1 for that bundle, for the version line your Licence Key states, under its Product
Schedule. It is part of your ELI v3 licence: it is not transferred separately from it.

## 4. Versions, updates and support

4.1 **Included updates.** Every maintenance and minor release in your Major Version Line is included
in your licence at no extra cost. For ELI v3 that is every 3.x release.

4.2 **Next major version.** The next major version (for example ELI v4) is a separate product and may
be sold as a paid upgrade. We may offer existing customers an upgrade discount.

4.3 **What you keep.** You may keep using any version you have received under your licence, for as
long as you want to, including after a later major version is released.

4.4 **Security fixes.** We will publish the support status of each Major Version Line. After the first
release of the next major version, we will continue to issue fixes for serious security
vulnerabilities in the previous line for at least **[to confirm: 12 months]**.

4.5 **Bundle compatibility.** Within a Major Version Line of ELI v3 we will aim to keep the bundle
and plugin interfaces compatible, and to announce any unavoidable change in advance.

4.6 **Support.** Support is as described in your Tier Supplement.

## 5. Activation and offline use

5.1 **Activation.** The Software may require you to enter a Licence Key. The key is checked on your
machine against a signature built into the Software. No connection to us is needed to activate it or
to keep using it.

5.2 **No continuous connection.** Ordinary use of the Software never requires a connection to us or
to any licence server.

5.3 **Reinstallation and recovery.** You may reinstall the Software and re-activate it after
reinstalling, after a hardware change or after replacing a machine. If you lose your Licence Key, or
it stops working on a machine you are entitled to use, contact us and we will help you recover access.

5.4 **No remote disablement.** We will not remotely disable or degrade a validly purchased ELI Product,
whether because time has passed, because a billing relationship has ended or for any other reason
outside §12. Withdrawing a Marketplace Package for security reasons (§10) is separate and does not
affect your ELI Product licence.

5.5 **Licence controls.** You may not bypass, disable or tamper with the Software's licence checks,
or use a Licence Key that was not issued to you.

## 6. Backups

You may make backup and archival copies of the Software and of Your Data. A backup copy may only be
used to restore a licensed installation.

## 7. Restrictions

Except as this agreement or your Tier Supplement expressly permits, you may not:

- copy, distribute, sell, rent, lend, lease or sublicense the Software, or any modified version of it;
- share, publish, sell or transfer your Licence Key, except as §3.6 allows;
- make the Software, or a service built on it, available to people outside your licence (for example
  as a hosted or multi-user service for third parties) unless your Tier Supplement, Product Schedule
  or a separate written agreement with us permits it;
- remove or alter copyright, licence or attribution notices; or
- use the Software to build a competing product offered to third parties.

**Reverse engineering.** You may not decompile, disassemble or reverse-engineer the Software, except
to the extent the law where you live gives you a right to do so that cannot be excluded by contract
(for example for interoperability). Nothing in this agreement removes such a right.

## 8. Your data and privacy

8.1 **Ownership.** You own or control Your Data. We claim no ownership of it and no licence to it.
Buying ELI does not give us any right in your memory database, documents or anything else you create.

8.2 **Local first.** The Software processes Your Data on your own machines. It contains no telemetry
and does not send Your Data to us. If a future feature would send any data to us, it will be off
unless you turn it on, and we will describe exactly what it sends.

8.3 **Purchase data.** For purchases we collect only what we need to take payment, issue and recover
Licence Keys, provide support, prevent fraud and meet legal obligations.

8.4 **Your responsibility.** You are responsible for keeping backups of Your Data and for the lawful
use of any personal data you process with the Software.

## 9. Third-party components and models

9.1 The Software includes third-party components under their own licences, listed in
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. Those licences govern those components, and nothing in this agreement
limits your rights under them.

9.2 AI models that you download or supply, including any suggested by the Software, are licensed by
their own authors under their own terms (see `models/MODEL_LICENSES.md`). You are responsible for
complying with them.

## 10. The marketplace and third-party packages

10.1 Marketplace Packages are not ELI Products. Each is licensed to you by its own publisher under the
publisher's own terms, and any purchase of one is between you and that publisher.

10.2 Review of a package by the ELI marketplace is a security review of that exact version. It is not
a warranty, a certification that the package is fit for any purpose, or proof of who the publisher is.

10.3 We may withdraw marketplace approval for a package, or warn about it or quarantine it, if we
find malicious behaviour, undisclosed permissions, infringement or a serious vulnerability. Where we
do, we will tell you why. We will not silently delete your files.

## 11. AI output

The Software produces output using AI models. Output can be incomplete, inaccurate or out of date.
It is not professional advice. You are responsible for checking output before relying on it and for
how you use it. A Product Schedule may add terms for its field.

## 12. Termination

12.1 We may end your licence only if you materially breach this agreement. If the breach can be put
right, we will first give you written notice and 30 days to put it right.

12.2 You may end your licence at any time by uninstalling the Software and deleting your copies.

12.3 When your licence ends you must stop using the Software and delete your copies. Sections 1, 3.3,
7, 8, 9 and 11–17 continue to apply.

## 13. Warranty

13.1 Nothing in this agreement limits rights you have as a consumer that cannot be excluded by law.

13.2 Subject to §13.1, the Software is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, express or
implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.
**[to confirm by solicitor for each target jurisdiction]**

## 14. Limitation of liability

14.1 Nothing in this agreement limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence,
for fraud, or for anything else that cannot be limited by law.

14.2 Subject to §14.1, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss, or
for loss of data, profits or business, arising from the Software.

14.3 Subject to §14.1, our total liability to you for an ELI Product is limited to the amount you paid
for that product's licence. **[to confirm by solicitor for each target jurisdiction]**

## 15. Changes to these terms

We may update these terms for future purchases. An update does not reduce the rights you already have
for a version you have already purchased, unless you agree to it.

## 16. Whole agreement

This agreement, your Tier Supplement, any applicable Product Schedule and your order or receipt are
the whole agreement between you and us about the ELI Product. If any part is found unenforceable, the
rest continues to apply.

## 17. Governing law

**[to confirm: governing law and courts.]** If you are a consumer, you also keep the protection of
